            <div xml:id="d315">

                <pb facs="0525" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg411"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/301: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-01T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 1,
                                1922—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>76. Your 150, October 26, 8 p.m. and 152 October 27 9 P.M.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d315-f1"/></p>
                <p>You may in your discretion orally and informally indicate to Greek authorities
                    that arbitrary action in the trial or execution of political prisoners in Greece
                    would in your own opinion undoubtedly make an unfortunate impression in this
                    country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
